    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="0884" n="872" xml:id="pg872"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/10–446: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bursley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-10-04">October 4,
                        1946</date>.<lb/>[Received October 5—2:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1075. Reply my query tonight re last paragraph Soviet note, Erkin said language
                    diabolically vague. He thinks object make Turks believe there will be conference
                    but what Soviets really seek is negotiations with Turks which if agreement
                    reached really decides outcome conference; if Turks Soviets failed reach accord
                    Soviets would say no use holding conference. Under this interpretation he thinks
                    matters little (mytel 1067<anchor n="89"
                        xml:id="d687-f1"/>) whether language relates conference under point 4 or
                    general one.</p>
                <p>Re timing Turk reply, he said still planned after meeting Cabinet. He made no
                    mention additional day or two (last paragraph mytel 1066<anchor n="90" xml:id="d687-f2"/>) but said his present
                    draft note was that to be presented Cabinet unless we or British had
                    suggestions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bursley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
